---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
const gallery = [
  { src: "/img/santa-cruz-village.jpg", alt: "Homes in the community of Santa Cruz", caption: "Santa Cruz, El Paraíso. 2021." },
  { src: "/img/santa-cruz-visit.jpg", alt: "A visit with a resident of the community", caption: "Field visit with residents. 2021." },
  { src: "/img/santa-cruz-clinic.jpg", alt: "A local health post", caption: "Local health services. 2021." },
  { src: "/img/santa-cruz-children.jpg", alt: "Children in the community", caption: "Children of Santa Cruz. 2021." },
];
---
<Base
  title="Our work"
  description="The Santa Cruz project in El Paraíso, Honduras: a five-year plan for water, agriculture, education and health, with the record of what was built."
  hero={true}
  heroImage="/img/santa-cruz-village.jpg"
>
  <div slot="hero" class="max-w-2xl">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold">Our work</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-white/85 leading-relaxed">
      What we planned, what was built, and where it stands today. Programs that are suspended are marked as suspended.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Section kicker="Honduras · 2020-2022 · suspended" title="The Santa Cruz project">
    <div class="prose-fbc text-[16px]">
      <p>
        Santa Cruz sits in the department of El Paraíso, Honduras. With the community we set three goals:
        end extreme poverty in Santa Cruz, bring the poverty rate down to 10 percent, and create direct
        local employment. For Better Community would walk alongside the community for five years, with
        specialists and technicians preparing residents to take full control at the end of that period.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-10">
      <video
        controls
        preload="none"
        poster="/img/santa-cruz-video-poster.jpg"
        class="w-full bg-navy-ink"
        width="1280" height="720"
      >
        <source src="/video/santa-cruz.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
        <track src="/video/santa-cruz.en.vtt" kind="subtitles" srclang="en" label="English" default />
        Your browser does not support embedded video.
      </video>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-[13px] text-slate">
        The Santa Cruz project, filmed on site in 2022. Spanish narration, with English subtitles
        adapted from the original. It presents the plan as it stood at the time, before the program
        was suspended.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="sand" kicker="The plan" title="Four tracks, one sequence">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="prose-fbc text-[15px]">
        <h3>Water first</h3>
        <p>
          Everything started with water, so the community would stop depending on the rainy season.
          Reservoirs on the high ground of the site, feeding lined ponds below.
        </p>
        <h3>Then food, from the same water</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Tilapia raised in the ponds</li>
          <li>Vegetables grown vertically above them, through hydroponics</li>
          <li>Cattle, pigs and poultry on dedicated ground</li>
          <li>Beekeeping, chosen so the wooded part of the land would be preserved</li>
          <li>An agro-industrial cooperative to hold it all, owned by the community</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="prose-fbc text-[15px]">
        <h3>Education, at every level</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Materials for preschool children, so they enter the system at all</li>
          <li>Teaching materials for primary school</li>
          <li>A trade school, and secondary students trained to administer the cooperative</li>
          <li>Support to the Álvaro Contreras school so it could restore its growing areas and feed its own students</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Women, money and health</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Support for women and young mothers as a central axis, not an afterthought</li>
          <li>Personal finance training, so families could manage and invest what they earned</li>
          <li>Preventive health care</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section kicker="Principle" title="Work in return">
    <div class="prose-fbc text-[16px]">
      <p>
        Every time residents received support, they gave a piece of work back to the community.
        Not as a condition imposed from outside, but so that what arrived was never a handout.
        It was earned, and it belonged to the people who earned it.
      </p>
      <p>
        That principle is the reason the plan reads the way it does. A cooperative rather than a
        distribution. A trade school rather than a scholarship. Ponds the community maintains rather
        than water trucked in.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="sand" kicker="On the ground" title="Santa Cruz, 2021">
    <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      {gallery.map((g) => (
        <figure>
          <img src={g.src} alt={g.alt} width="1400" height="930" class="w-full h-56 object-cover" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption class="mt-2 text-[13px] text-slate">{g.caption}</figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))}
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section kicker="Status" title="Where the project stands">
    <div class="prose-fbc text-[16px]">
      <p>
        The program is suspended. Following a change of national administration in Honduras, the
        institutional conditions and approvals this kind of work depends on are no longer in place.
        We took the decision to pause rather than continue a program we could not deliver to the standard
        the community was promised.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing was abandoned. We hold the plan, the engineering studies, the site assessment, the
        relationships and the record, and we will resume if conditions allow.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="sand" kicker="2019 · completed" title="Deep-water reef research">
    <div class="prose-fbc text-[16px]">
      <p>
        Volunteer technical divers assisted a university research team by recovering deep-water coral reef
        samples from a wreck, to help document how those reefs function. Reefs sit at the base of a food
        chain that coastal families depend on for both food and income, which is why a marine research
        dive belongs in the work of an organization focused on self-sufficiency.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section kicker="Guatemala · 2020" title="NGO law analysis">
    <div class="prose-fbc text-[16px]">
      <p>
        We published an analysis of changes to the law governing nongovernmental organizations in Guatemala,
        what those changes required of organizations working there, and what they would mean for the
        communities those organizations serve. It is archived in our
        <a href="/field-notes/">field notes</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
